1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,200
This is the Wall of DOPEMIND,

2
00:00:02,399 --> 00:00:04,679
newly claimed on cents.vision.

3
00:00:05,025 --> 00:00:05,919
Its signature Cent

4
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:09,439
is number 478, from 1963.

5
00:00:09,512 --> 00:00:11,119
In the Numismatists Discord,

6
00:00:11,199 --> 00:00:12,320
DOPEMIND asked:

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,400
"What should I add to expand the set?

8
00:00:14,519 --> 00:00:16,800
Wondering about the direction for this collection."

9
00:00:16,879 --> 00:00:18,693
As of November 2026,

10
00:00:18,746 --> 00:00:23,126
the Wall holds 12 Cents, from 1963 to 1981.

11
00:00:23,199 --> 00:00:27,120
Eight carry a patina: verdigris, obsidian or desert.

12
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:28,399
What it does not hold:

13
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,399
a red patina, a wheat penny,

14
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:33,926
or a Cent from 1969 or 1971.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,159
centoshi replied: "You already know

16
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:39,847
my answer." DOPEMIND wrote back: "1971."

17
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:43,159
centoshi holds 16 Cents from 1971,

18
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,966
more than any other collector.

19
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:47,627
Of 1971, Martin Lehnen wrote:

20
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:49,679
"It was the year the United States abandoned

21
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:51,759
the gold standard, severing the connection

22
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,093
between currency and tangible value."

23
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:58,200
A 1971 Cent would add the 1971 Club badge.

24
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,027
With the Wall's 1979,

25
00:01:00,052 --> 00:01:03,286
it would leave a Chronicle Set one 1982 short.

26
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:05,253
Daidatep suggested six Cents,

27
00:01:05,307 --> 00:01:07,686
and added: "I could go on and on."

28
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:11,079
Number 8657 is from 1965.

29
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:13,680
Only 90 Cents are from 1965,

30
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:16,326
fewer than any other year of the 1960s.

31
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:20,400
Number 8820, from 1972, carries red patina.

32
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,947
With all four base patinas,

33
00:01:21,972 --> 00:01:23,766
the card would add a Patina Set.

34
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:26,692
Number 6451 is from 1980.

35
00:01:26,746 --> 00:01:28,346
With the Wall's 1981,

36
00:01:28,373 --> 00:01:31,766
it would leave a 1980s Set one 1982 short.

37
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,959
Number 6875, from 1967,

38
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:37,546
is heavily abraded, one of 44.

39
00:01:37,572 --> 00:01:38,599
In the Traits Atlas,

40
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,686
heavy abrasion "dominates the read of the coin."

41
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:45,572
Number 6782, a 1969 from Denver,

42
00:01:45,626 --> 00:01:47,927
would add the 1969 Club badge.

43
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,546
And number 5888, a 1956 from Denver,

44
00:01:51,572 --> 00:01:53,704
would be the Wall's first wheat penny.

45
00:01:53,974 --> 00:01:55,120
Find all of the Collector Walls

46
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,439
on cents.vision under Collectors.

47
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,760
What should DOPEMIND add next?

48
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,200
Tell us what you think.
